China is rejecting calls to slow its artificial intelligence, or ai, development just weeks before a planned summit with the United States. This is Omni View, episode 181. Chinese officials have said they will not pause or limit advances in the field, and they have put that position on the record ahead of an expected meeting between President Xi Jinping and President Trump. Reports indicate Beijing views continued ai progress as essential to its national priorities.

